{
  "title": "THA Dislocation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/5012/tha-dislocation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 23 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "THA Dislocation is a complication following THA and may occur due to patient noncomplicance with post-operative restrictions, implant malposition, or soft-tissue deficiency.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs of the hip. CT of the pelvis can assist with assessing for implant malpositioning.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is closed reduction of the hip. Surgical management with possible revision THA is indicated for irreducible dislocations, recurrent instability, and implant malposition.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1-3%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "70% occur within first month",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "75-90% posterior",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**anterior**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extension and external rotation of hip",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**posterior**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "flexion, internal rotation, adduction of hip",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "prior hip surgery (greatest risk factor)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "conflicting evidence regarding patient gender",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "higher comorbidity burden",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "BMI < 20 or > 35",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use of meta-on-poly or metal-on-metal bearing surfaces",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use of cemented components",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior surgical approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**repairing capsule** and r**econstructing external rotators** brings dislocation rate close to anterior approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "malpositioning of components",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ideal positioning of acetabular component is **40 degrees of abduction** and **15 degrees anteversion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in general, excessive anteversion increases risk of anterior hip dislocation; excessive retroversion increases risk of posterior hip dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "spastic or neuromuscular disease (Parkinson's)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "drug or alcohol abuse",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased femoral offset (decreases tissue tension and stability)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased femoral head to neck ratio",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "prior spinal fusion or fixed spinopelvic alignment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "polyethylene wear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "common cause of late instability occuring >5 years after procedure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often reports activity that puts patient in a position that provokes dislocation (hip flexion, adduction, internal rotation)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "shoe tying",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sitting in low seat or toilet",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cross-table lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increased acetabular inclination > 60°",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increased acetabular anteversion > 20°",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "aceabular retroversion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "look for **eccentric position of femoral head** as an indication of polyethylene wear and risk for impending dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "to assess for implant malposition",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction and immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "two-thirds of early dislocations can be treated with closed reduction and immobilization",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "immobilize with hip spica cast, hip abduction brace, or knee immobilizer",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "polyethylene exchange",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "stable well-aligned implants with extensive polyethylene wear thought to be sole reason for dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "revision THA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indicated if 2 or more dislocations with evidence of",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**implant malalignment**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "vertical acetabular component",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "acetabular retroversion",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**implant failure**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**polyethylene wear**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "techniques",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "see below",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "conversion to hemiarthroplasty with larger femoral head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "for soft tissue deficiency or dysfunction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contraindicated if acetabular bone is compromised",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "older technique rarely used with development of dual mobility implants",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "resection arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "when all options have been exhausted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "significant bone loss and soft tissue deficiency",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**psychiatric patients** who are dislocating for secondary gain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Revision THA**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "techniques to prevent future dislocation during THA include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**realign components**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indicated if malalignment explains dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "retroverted acetabulum",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "vertical acetabulum",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "short femoral neck",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "lack of femoral neck offset",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "retroverted femoral component",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**head enlargement**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "optimize head-neck ratio",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**utilization of a lateralized liner**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increases femoral offset",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**trochanteric osteotomy and advancement**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "places abductor complex under tension which increases hip compression force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**conversion to a constrained acetabular component**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "recurrent instability with a **well positioned acetabular component** due to soft tissue deficiency or dysfunction",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**conversion to dual mobility (DM) implant**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "consists of a small femoral head captive and mobile within a polyethylene liner",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Due to a more favorable (effective) head-neck ratio, dual mobility cups permit a larger range of motion compared to fixed-liner implants",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "DM have unique risk for intraprosthetic dislocation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**conversion to tripolar construct**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
